  "notes": [
    "Plan applicable to students who joined the program in Fall 2025 or later (AY 2026/2027), Department of Applied Biology, College of Sciences. Three concentrations in the fourth year (A Forensic & Medical Biotechnology, B Industrial Biotechnology, C Plant & Environmental Biotechnology), tagged in 'track'; courses with track null are common to all concentrations.",
    "No overall credit-hour total is printed. Semester totals plus the 3-credit Field training add up to 124 for each concentration (years 1-3 = 97, field training 3, fourth year 24).",
    "type_raw holds the requirement category from the compulsory-courses tables (University Required, College of Sciences Required, Supporting Required, Program Compulsory) or the elective tables (University Required (Elective), Program Elective).",
    "1450399 Field training: 6 weeks during the summer, 3 credit hours (prerequisite: 65 credit hours + 1450361 + 1450352); placed after the third year.",
    "AI and Digital Technologies is printed with two codes: 1501110 (E) for the English section and 1501111 (A) for the Arabic section. Arabic Language is 0201102, or 0201105 (Arabic Language for non-Arabic Speakers).",
    "Courses marked with * in the PDF are required for the Pre-Medical Track (with the core curriculum they satisfy common medical-school prerequisites for the MCAT or equivalent). Starred in the plan: General Physics for (HS), General Chemistry (HS), General Biology (1), General Biology (2), General Biology Lab, Organic Chemistry (HS), Cell Biology, General Biochemistry and General Biochemistry Lab; General Chemistry II, Organic Chemistry II, Physics II (and labs) are starred among the program electives. Non-Biotechnology students on the Pre-Medical Track must complete all starred courses plus Cell Biology Lab (1450252). Introduction to Psychology (0206103) is required for students on the Pre-Medical Track.",
    "University electives: one course from Domain F, one from Domain G and one from Domain H. Students in programs taught in Arabic cannot register for electives taught in English. The domain course lists are included as catalogue rows (year null).",
    "Program elective courses: 12 credit hours. Rows with year null are catalogue lists (program electives and university-elective domains) and are not placed in a semester.",
    "Prerequisite inconsistency in the PDF: in the 'Program Compulsory Courses (For all concentrations)' table (page 4) the prerequisite column of 1450331, 1450332, 1450333, 1450336, 1450341 and 1450342 repeats the course's own code. The study-plan tables (page 1) give the sensible prerequisites (e.g. 1450251 for 1450331) and are used here.",
    "Prerequisite '-' is an empty list; a blank prerequisite cell (departmental electives) is null. 'Cor' means co-requisite."
  ]
}